+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# Resource integrity verification
+#
+# Several resources are fetched at runtime from this repository (raw.github
+# usercontent.com, or the GitHub Pages mirror) and are then either executed
+# directly as PowerShell (installer language files), or injected as JavaScript
+# / CSS into the Spotify client, or used as JSON instructions that drive byte-
+# level patching of the Spotify client. If any single one of those files were
+# modified on the server without run.ps1 itself being modified, this script
+# would previously execute or inject that modified content without any check.
+#
+# $script:IntegrityManifest pins the SHA-256 hash of every such file as it
+# existed when this copy of run.ps1 was released. Assert-TrustedResource
+# verifies newly downloaded bytes against that pinned hash before they are
+# ever executed, injected, or parsed as patch instructions. A mismatch is
+# treated as fatal for that resource: SpotifyPlus will refuse to use it and
+# will tell the user to update to the latest run.ps1 instead of silently
+# proceeding.
+#
+# Scope and limits (please read before assuming this "fully" secures the
+# install):
+#   - This only covers files hosted in THIS repository. It intentionally does
+#     NOT attempt to verify the LoaderSpot/table version manifest or the
+#     Spotify installer binary itself, because this repository has no
+#     authority to publish a trusted hash for content it does not own -
+#     doing so would be a false sense of security. See downloadSp() for the
+#     separate, weaker (size-only) check that applies to the Spotify
+#     installer, and README "Security" for why a cryptographic check is not
+#     currently possible there.
+#   - This manifest is only as trustworthy as the copy of run.ps1 the user
+#     obtained in the first place. run.ps1 itself is not code-signed and is
+#     fetched over plain HTTPS by Install_*.bat/Uninstall.bat without a
+#     separate signature check. That remains a residual, documented risk -
+#     see README "Security".
+#   - Every dated release of SpotifyPlus regenerates this manifest from the
+#     files actually shipped in that release via
+#     scripts/Update-IntegrityManifest.ps1. If you edit any of the files
+#     listed below, re-run that script before publishing, or every user's
+#     next run will hard-fail the integrity check for that file.
